    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1201">

                <pb facs="1591" n="1581" xml:id="pg1581"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Germany)/12–1445</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Note by the Allied
                            Secretariat to the Control Council, Allied
                            Control Authority
                    </hi><anchor n="77" xml:id="d1201-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">CONL/P/45/63</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-11-28">28 November 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Report of the Air Directorate on the Creation of a
                        System of Air Corridors for Flights Between the Zones of Occupation in
                        Germany</hi>
                </p>
                <p>At its Twenty-third meeting the Coordinating Committee considered the report of
                    the Air Directorate on the creation of a system of air corridors for flights
                    between the Zones of occupation in Germany and approved the creation of the
                    three following air corridors from Berlin to the west:</p>
                <p>Berlin–Hamburg, Berlin–Bückeburg and Berlin–Frankfurt-on-Main.</p>
                <p>As regards the request of the Directorate for a decision on the question of
                    creating corridors as follows:</p>
                <p>Berlin–Warsaw, Berlin–Prague, Berlin–Copenhagen and Bückeburg–Prague, the
                    Coordinating Committee decided that this question did not fall within its
                    competence and must be settled at the Governmental level.</p>
                <p>In accordance with Conclusion 309 of the Minutes of the Coordinating Committee
                    meeting of the 27th November (CORC/M(45)23) the attached document<anchor n="78"
                        xml:id="d1201-f2"/> is submitted for the consideration of the Control
                    Council at their Thirteenth meeting on the 30th November, 1945.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>S. M. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kudriavtsev</hi>
                    </signed>, <hi rendition="#italic">1st Sec’y</hi>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>H. A. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gerhardt</hi>
                    </signed>, <hi rendition="#italic">Colonel</hi>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>T. N. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grazebrook</hi>
                    </signed>, <hi rendition="#italic">Brigadier</hi>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Monsieur</hi> L. J. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Calvy</hi>
                    </signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Allied Secretariat</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1201-f1" n="77" type="source" xml:id="d1201-f1-content">
                <p>Copy transmitted to the Department as an enclosure to despatch 1498, December 14,
                    from Berlin, not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1201-f2" n="78" xml:id="d1201-f2-content">
                <p>The text, which is virtually identical with that of the Annex to CORC/P(45)170,
                    November 22, is printed in <hi rendition="#italic">Documents on Germany,
                        1944–1961</hi>, (87th Cong., 1st sess., Committee Print for the Senate
                    Committee on Foreign Relations, December 1961), p. 45.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
